{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "03300",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.78,
      "end_seconds": 6.89,
      "duration_seconds": 6.11,
      "text": "Oh, um, hi, doctor, I hope I'm not disturbing you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.91,
      "end_seconds": 11.75,
      "duration_seconds": 3.84,
      "text": "Yes, have a seat. Tell me what's going on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 13.63,
      "end_seconds": 17.82,
      "duration_seconds": 4.19,
      "text": "Well, I've been having a severe headache for days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 21.98,
      "end_seconds": 26.29,
      "duration_seconds": 4.31,
      "text": "Let me get the readings out of the way."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 36.37,
      "end_seconds": 38.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.29,
      "text": "Okay, this won't take long..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 49.45,
      "end_seconds": 59.45,
      "duration_seconds": 10.0,
      "text": "Okay: pulse 81, blood pressure 153 over 104. And temperature 36.9, saturation 98 percent. What's the timeline, when did it begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 60.91,
      "end_seconds": 65.08,
      "duration_seconds": 4.17,
      "text": "Actually, it's been one week, I'm fairly sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 65.43,
      "end_seconds": 76.3,
      "duration_seconds": 10.87,
      "text": "Okay, go on. Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 82.23,
      "end_seconds": 97.81,
      "duration_seconds": 15.58,
      "text": "Yes, lying down. That makes it worse. I'd call it moderate. My family kept telling me to get it checked. I didn't want to bother you but it keeps coming back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 105.11,
      "end_seconds": 108.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.38,
      "text": "Did you get head injury or fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 110.32,
      "end_seconds": 113.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "No, I'd have said so."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 115.03,
      "end_seconds": 118.99,
      "duration_seconds": 3.96,
      "text": "And weakness on one side, any of that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 120.6,
      "end_seconds": 125.23,
      "duration_seconds": 4.63,
      "text": "I mean, no, none, no weakness on one side."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 126.48,
      "end_seconds": 129.94,
      "duration_seconds": 3.46,
      "text": "On the cardiac side, anything I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 132.48,
      "end_seconds": 135.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "Well, no, nothing with my heart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 143.29,
      "end_seconds": 145.46,
      "duration_seconds": 2.17,
      "text": "Tell me your medicines, please."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 147.31,
      "end_seconds": 159.41,
      "duration_seconds": 12.1,
      "text": "Oh, I take apixaban, 5 milligrams, twice a day for the heart rhythm. I wasn't sure whether to come in at all, to be honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 159.66,
      "end_seconds": 160.36,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Understood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 161.18,
      "end_seconds": 163.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "The contraceptive pill, daily."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 165.21,
      "end_seconds": 166.69,
      "duration_seconds": 1.48,
      "text": "What's your work?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 168.61,
      "end_seconds": 172.32,
      "duration_seconds": 3.71,
      "text": "I'm a plumber, lots of bending and kneeling."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 172.94,
      "end_seconds": 176.77,
      "duration_seconds": 3.83,
      "text": "What does a normal day of food look like?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 182.96,
      "end_seconds": 186.93,
      "duration_seconds": 3.97,
      "text": "Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 188.36,
      "end_seconds": 190.57,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "So, how active are you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 192.35,
      "end_seconds": 196.09,
      "duration_seconds": 3.74,
      "text": "I hardly move around during the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 197.95,
      "end_seconds": 200.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "Has anyone ever diagnosed you with something?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 202.87,
      "end_seconds": 206.18,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "An irregular heartbeat, for about ten years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 208.25,
      "end_seconds": 212.4,
      "duration_seconds": 4.15,
      "text": "Alright, an irregular heartbeat, that matches what I have here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 224.45,
      "end_seconds": 227.73,
      "duration_seconds": 3.28,
      "text": "Right, before we go further, any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 229.69,
      "end_seconds": 234.82,
      "duration_seconds": 5.13,
      "text": "I, I don't think I have any, um, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 235.92,
      "end_seconds": 238.11,
      "duration_seconds": 2.19,
      "text": "May I examine you now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 239.25,
      "end_seconds": 240.51,
      "duration_seconds": 1.26,
      "text": "Look straight ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 255.03,
      "end_seconds": 258.7,
      "duration_seconds": 3.67,
      "text": "The optic discs look swollen and you are drowsy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 263.28,
      "end_seconds": 265.29,
      "duration_seconds": 2.01,
      "text": "You can sit up now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 283.63,
      "end_seconds": 296.56,
      "duration_seconds": 12.93,
      "text": "So where does that leave us? I don't have a clear answer today: possible cerebral venous thrombosis is possible, and so is raised pressure in the head."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 298.38,
      "end_seconds": 299.73,
      "duration_seconds": 1.35,
      "text": "Is this permanent?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 301.26,
      "end_seconds": 330.78,
      "duration_seconds": 29.52,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like possible cerebral venous thrombosis, but I'd like to confirm. Let's book an MRI of the head to look into papilloedema. Let's book an urgent CT venogram to look into possible venous thrombosis. Stop the pill, you need an urgent scan and admission. Avoid taking any extra painkillers on top of what I'm prescribing without checking with us."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 331.39,
      "end_seconds": 344.37,
      "duration_seconds": 12.98,
      "text": "The thing that would worry me is if the symptoms get worse. If that happens, go to emergency. Let's review you straight away. I think we're done unless you have questions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 345.2,
      "end_seconds": 347.49,
      "duration_seconds": 2.29,
      "text": "Thank you, that's helpful."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 349.39,
      "end_seconds": 350.64,
      "duration_seconds": 1.25,
      "text": "Look after yourself."
    }
  ]
}